{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AjPk6TuBaTNr7N6sggkcFB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 145,\n3\t \"title\": \"Allow monospaced digit fonts for menu item labels on macOS\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Problem Description\\n\\nOn macOS, menu item labels are rendered with the system menu font, whose digits are proportional. So any menu showing a column of numbers comes out jagged, because e.g. `11:15` renders narrower than `09:45`:\\n\\n<img width=\\\"214\\\" height=\\\"121\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28269fc6-8033-4065-8e63-0782f94198f0\\\" />\\n\\nThere's currently no way around this: `MenuItem.label` maps to `NSMenuItem.title`, and Electron exposes neither `attributedTitle` nor any font option. In a native app this is a one-liner: set `attributedTitle` with `monospacedDigitSystemFontOfSize:`, the SF variant with tabular figures that's otherwise identical to the menu font.\\n\\n#22363 solved the same problem for the tray title with `tray.setTitle(title, { fontType: 'monospacedDigit' })`. Menu item labels never got the equivalent, so a tray calendar can align its countdown but not the time column in its dropdown.\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nThe same `fontType` option on `MenuItem`, macOS-only like `toolTip`:\\n\\n```js\\nnew MenuItem({\\n  label: \\\"11:15  Doctor's appointment\\\",\\n  fontType: 'monospacedDigit'\\n})\\n```\\n\\nThe implementation looks small: when the option is set, `electron_menu_controller.mm` renders the label via `attributedTitle` with the corresponding font variant, analogous to the `fontType` handling in `tray_icon_cocoa.mm`. Supporting both tray values (`monospaced` and `monospacedDigit`) keeps the two APIs symmetric.\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\n- Padding with figure spaces (U+2007): Still unequal widths, the digits themselves are proportional\\n- Unicode fullwidth/monospace digits: Wrong font, looks out of place\\n- Pre-rendering the time column into template `NativeImage` icons: What we ship today – works well, but adds a lot of machinery for one line of AppKit\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nI attached [menu-item-font-type.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29671470/menu-item-font-type.patch) mirroring the `toolTip` per-item plumbing and the tray `fontType` implementation. It was drafted with Claude Fable 5, and I'm currently unable to build Electron locally – so it's untested. Happy to open a PR from it so CI can validate it, or for a maintainer to adopt or rework it instead.\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"enhancement :sparkles:\"\n7\t ],\n8\t \"state\": \"open\",\n9\t \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n10\t \"as_of\": \"2026-07-05T08:53:18Z\",\n11\t \"replay\": true\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93a669cf-4792-43ec-9346-b9352b1c3b22","uuid":"0ed94821-c654-46a1-9363-d6ca2e48ad22","timestamp":"2026-10-23T12:34:15.564Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 145,\n \"title\": \"Allow monospaced digit fonts for menu item labels on macOS\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Problem Description\\n\\nOn macOS, menu item labels are rendered with the system menu font, whose digits are proportional. So any menu showing a column of numbers comes out jagged, because e.g. `11:15` renders narrower than `09:45`:\\n\\n<img width=\\\"214\\\" height=\\\"121\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28269fc6-8033-4065-8e63-0782f94198f0\\\" />\\n\\nThere's currently no way around this: `MenuItem.label` maps to `NSMenuItem.title`, and Electron exposes neither `attributedTitle` nor any font option. In a native app this is a one-liner: set `attributedTitle` with `monospacedDigitSystemFontOfSize:`, the SF variant with tabular figures that's otherwise identical to the menu font.\\n\\n#22363 solved the same problem for the tray title with `tray.setTitle(title, { fontType: 'monospacedDigit' })`. Menu item labels never got the equivalent, so a tray calendar can align its countdown but not the time column in its dropdown.\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nThe same `fontType` option on `MenuItem`, macOS-only like `toolTip`:\\n\\n```js\\nnew MenuItem({\\n  label: \\\"11:15  Doctor's appointment\\\",\\n  fontType: 'monospacedDigit'\\n})\\n```\\n\\nThe implementation looks small: when the option is set, `electron_menu_controller.mm` renders the label via `attributedTitle` with the corresponding font variant, analogous to the `fontType` handling in `tray_icon_cocoa.mm`. Supporting both tray values (`monospaced` and `monospacedDigit`) keeps the two APIs symmetric.\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\n- Padding with figure spaces (U+2007): Still unequal widths, the digits themselves are proportional\\n- Unicode fullwidth/monospace digits: Wrong font, looks out of place\\n- Pre-rendering the time column into template `NativeImage` icons: What we ship today – works well, but adds a lot of machinery for one line of AppKit\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nI attached [menu-item-font-type.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29671470/menu-item-font-type.patch) mirroring the `toolTip` per-item plumbing and the tray `fontType` implementation. It was drafted with Claude Fable 5, and I'm currently unable to build Electron locally – so it's untested. Happy to open a PR from it so CI can validate it, or for a maintainer to adopt or rework it instead.\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"enhancement :sparkles:\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-07-05T08:53:18Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AjPk6TuBaTNr7N6sggkcFB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
